=== HTML ===
<style>
	/* No download at all: the reader's own system font */
	.system {
		font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
	}

	/* Loading a font file you host yourself.
	   Drag a .woff2 into this editor, then uncomment this block. */
	/* @font-face {
		font-family: "My Font";
		src: url("myfont.woff2") format("woff2");
		font-weight: 100 900;
		font-display: swap;
	}
	h1 {
		font-family: "My Font", system-ui, sans-serif;
	} */

	body {
		margin: 16px;
		line-height: 1.5;
		font-family: Georgia, serif;
	}
	h1 {
		font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
	}
</style>

<h1>A heading, waiting for a font</h1>

<p class="system">
	This paragraph uses system-ui, which is whatever font your device already
	uses for its own interface. It loads instantly, because there is nothing
	to load.
</p>

<p>
	This one falls back to Georgia. Drag a <strong>.woff2</strong> file into
	this editor, uncomment the block above, and change the filename to try
	your own!
</p>
